---
title: Post single
layout: home
description: The one post layout. Two columns — the post on the left, the rail on the right, contents first — and the head sits on the post's own column, so the hero and the body share an edge.
eyebrow: Collections · Post
source: src/layout/page.css · components/post-hero.css · content.css · widget.css
---
<section class="im-section im-wrap im-pt-sm im-section-sm">
	<p class="im-eyebrow">Collections · Post · {{page.title}}</p>
	<p class="im-lede">{{page.description}}</p>
	<p class="doc-source"><code>{{page.source}}</code></p>
</section>

<div class="im-single im-wrap-wide" id="single" data-sidebar="on">
	<article class="im-stack im-stack-md">
		{{#with demo.post}}{{> "components/post-hero" id="post-hero" style="stack" crumbs=true zoom=true section="Writing" section_url="/collections/post/"}}{{/with}}

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush" data-toc-skip>
			<details class="im-toc-inline">
				<summary>Contents <span>On this page</span></summary>
				<div class="im-toc" data-toc="#single"></div>
			</details>
		</section>

		<section class="im-content im-content-flush im-content-lede im-content-dropcap" id="post-body" data-im-zoom>
			<p>Sorrento to Amalfi is forty kilometres and takes two hours, because nobody on it wants to arrive. The road was cut into the cliff in the 1840s and has not been widened since; buses fold their mirrors in to pass.</p>
			<h2>Three widths, one grid</h2>
			<p>The wrapper is a grid with named lines — <code>full</code>, <code>wide</code>, <code>main</code>. Every child lands in <code>main</code>; a card the author set to <em>wide</em> or <em>full</em> in the editor carries a class that moves it outward. No negative margins, no <code>100vw</code>.</p>
			<figure class="kg-card kg-image-card kg-width-wide kg-card-hascaption"><img src="{{demo.three.[0].feature_image}}" class="kg-image" alt="A village on a cliff above the sea" loading="lazy" width="1600" height="900"><figcaption><span>A <strong>wide</strong> image: past the text on each side while there is room. The frame in its corner opens it.</span></figcaption></figure>
			<h2>What the road actually costs</h2>
			<p>Ten euro an hour is the published parking price in Positano and fifteen is the August one. The SITA bus is ten euro for the day and somebody else does the parking. Every number from four days is in the <a href="/collections/travel/trip/">itinerary</a>.</p>
			<aside class="im-ad im-ad-inread im-ad-inread-text" aria-label="Advertisement"><span class="im-ad-label">Sponsored</span><img src="{{demo.shots.[3]}}" alt="" loading="lazy"><b>Ghost hosting that does not oversell the box</b><span>Two CPUs, real backups, a support inbox a person reads.</span></aside>
			<h2>East to west, sea side</h2>
			<p>Drive it east to west and you are on the sea side of the road for the whole two hours, which is a completely different drive from the cliff side. The bus drivers fold their mirrors in without slowing down, which I am still thinking about.</p>
			<blockquote class="kg-blockquote-alt">Nobody on this road wants to arrive.</blockquote>
			<h3>If you only have one day</h3>
			<p>Sorrento to Positano and back on the bus. Everything after Positano is better with a night in it.</p>
			<h2>What I would do differently</h2>
			<ul><li>Two nights in Positano, not one.</li><li>Skip the car after Amalfi.</li><li>Go in November.</li></ul>
		</section>

		{{> "components/post-footer" author=false support=true newsletter=true nav=true related=demo.three related_url="/collections/post/"}}
		{{> "components/comments" thread=demo.comments count="41"}}
	</article>

	<aside>
		<div class="im-sticky-rail">
			<div class="im-widgets">
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="w-toc">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="w-toc">On this page</h2>
					<div class="im-toc" data-toc="#post-body"></div>
				</section>
				{{#with demo.author}}{{> "components/author" status="Open to work"}}{{/with}}
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="w-series">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="w-series">This series <a href="/collections/series/">4 parts</a></h2>
					<ol class="im-timeline im-timeline-detailed im-widget-series">
						{{#each demo.series}}
						<li class="im-timeline-item" data-state="{{state}}">
							<span class="im-timeline-marker">{{part}}</span>
							<time class="im-timeline-time">{{when}}</time>
							<h3 class="im-timeline-title">{{#if url}}<a href="{{url}}">{{title}}</a>{{else}}<span>{{title}}</span>{{/if}}</h3>
						</li>
						{{/each}}
					</ol>
				</section>
				<section class="im-widget" aria-labelledby="w-about">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="w-about">About this post</h2>
					<dl class="im-widget-facts"><dt>Published</dt><dd>17 Sep 2026</dd><dt>Updated</dt><dd>21 Sep 2026</dd><dt>Reading</dt><dd>6 min</dd><dt>Filed under</dt><dd><a href="/collections/tag/page/">Travel</a></dd></dl>
				</section>
				<section class="im-widget im-widget-fill" aria-labelledby="w-sub">
					<h2 class="im-widget-title" id="w-sub">The letter</h2>
					<p class="im-widget-heading">A post a fortnight, and what it cost.</p>
					{{> "components/subscribe" id="post-email" button="Join"}}
				</section>
				<aside class="im-ad im-ad-rectangle" aria-label="Advertisement"><span class="im-ad-label">Sponsored</span><span class="im-ad-slot"><img src="{{demo.shots.[5]}}" alt="" loading="lazy"></span><button class="im-btn im-btn-sm im-ad-remove" type="button" popovertarget="ad-gate">{{icon "circle-x"}}Remove ads</button></aside>
			</div>
		</div>
	</aside>
</div>

<section class="im-section im-wrap"><div class="im-prose">
<p>One layout for a post. The head is <code>im-posthero</code> on the article's own column, so its left edge is the body's; the rail is <code>im-sticky-rail</code> with the contents first, the author (opens), the series as a detailed timeline, the facts, the letter, one ad. <code>data-sidebar="off"</code> on <code>im-single</code> drops the rail for a post that wants the full measure. On a phone the contents sit inline under the head.</p>
</div></section>
